# BFF Service Rules for AI Assistant

## Critical Terminology
- ALWAYS use "User" - NEVER use "RecipientSigner" or "Recipient" in backend code
- Database table is `users` (NOT `recipient_signers` or `recipients`)
- Entity class is `User` (NOT `RecipientSigner` or `Recipient`)
- API endpoints use `/users` (NOT `/recipient-signers` or `/recipients`)

## Database
- Use Oracle Database for all persistence
- Spring Session stored in Oracle DB (Spring Session JDBC)
- Transaction metadata in Oracle DB

## Architecture
- Spring Boot BFF service
- Session management via Spring Session (Oracle)
- CSRF protection enabled
- Mock Ping authentication (will integrate real Ping later)
- Integrates with: eSignature Backend, Alert Service, Branding Service

## Code Style
- Use Java naming conventions
- Use DTOs for API requests/responses
- Validate all inputs
- Handle service integration failures gracefully
- Log transaction state changes

## Key Patterns
- Store transaction metadata locally for fast queries
- Sync with eSignature backend asynchronously
- Account-based data filtering

